Reckless Technology toolkit - third-party parts

The toolkit ships no binary of its own: it is source, built into the company's products, and each product's release
carries the full third-party notices of everything in its binaries (vst-plugins' THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, written by
its tools/third_party_notices.py from the trees its build fetched and the pins below). This file says what of the
toolkit is another's, so a product's notices can name all of it.

Fetched at configure time, never committed, each pinned by a tag, version or commit in cmake/ToolkitPins.cmake (which
the toolkit hands up to a product as RECKLESS_TOOLKIT_PINS) and by its archive's hash where it is fetched:

  Skia, with skcms (skia-pack's prebuilt release)  BSD 3-clause         the GUI's canvas (skia/, gfx/skia/)
  libpng, zlib (from the skia-pack release)        libpng, zlib         Skia's PNG codec and encoder
  zlib's SIMD routines (the Chromium source tree)  BSD 3-clause         inside the skia-pack's zlib
  FreeType (from the skia-pack release, Linux)     FreeType Licence     Skia's fonts on Linux
  Steinberg ASIO SDK (Windows)                     Steinberg's ASIO     ASIO devices (audio/win/AsioDevice.cpp): its
                                                   licence              host files (asio.cpp, asiodrivers.cpp,
                                                                        asiolist.cpp) compiled in, reckless_asio_host;
                                                                        its source never distributed in part or whole
  Monocypher                                       BSD 2-clause or CC0  a licence's Ed25519 check (licence/)
  dr_flac, dr_mp3 (dr_libs)                        public domain or     audio files (core/AudioFiles.h)
                                                   MIT No Attribution
  stb_vorbis (stb)                                 public domain or MIT audio files (core/AudioFiles.h)
  GoogleTest                                       BSD 3-clause         the suites alone, in no product binary

